  "english": "And they came to the tomb. Eve of the Fast of the Holy Cross.\n6. Monday. Tone [BK]. Fast of the Holy Cross. Canticle of the youths [Harts] [BK]: \"Lord God of our fathers.\"\n8. Wednesday. Tone [DK]. Fast. Feast of the Birth of the Holy Virgin from Anna.\n12. Sunday. Tone [AK]. Exaltation of the Cross. See up to the eleventh Sunday in the First Volume. But for the [Harts] canticles of the martyrs and of the fasts, the Sunday resurrection evening hymns [Hambartsi], and those of the same days, and the Saturday feasts, look at the 40th year-letter, keeping the order of this month.\n\nNovember:\n21. Sunday. Tone [DK]. Eleventh. Feast of the Presentation of the Mother of God. Eve of the Fifty Days Fast [Yisnakats].\n22. Monday. Tone [AZ]. Fast of the Fifty Days. Canticle of the youths [Harts] [GD]: \"Blessed art thou forever.\"\n28. Sunday. Tone [DZ]. First. Canticle of the youths [Harts] [AK]: \"Unoriginate Word.\" Evening hymn [Hamb.] [G3]: \"You who from above.\"\n29. Monday. Tone [DK]. [Feast of] Julian and Basil, and of Indus and Domna, etc. Canticle of the youths [Harts] [DZ]: \"Holy art thou, Lord.\" See also the others in the First Volume, keeping the order of this place.\n\nDecember:\n5. Sunday. Tone [GK]. Second. Canticle of the youths [Harts] [BZ]: \"Who art king.\" Evening hymn [Hamb.] [GK]: \"Having taken also our [likeness].\"\n6. Monday. Tone [DZ]. [Feast of] Gennadius and Mercurius, and of Jacob [Yakovik] and of Irava-parats [the orthodox].\n7. Tuesday. Tone [DK]. Canticle of the youths [Harts] of the Egyptians: Paul, Pola, etc.\n9. Thursday. Tone [AK]. Feast of the Conception of the Holy Virgin by Anna.\n12. Sunday. Tone [GD]. Third. Canticle of the youths [Harts] [BK]: \"Unoriginate God.\" Evening hymn [Hamb.] [G3]: \"Glorified is thy.\" Eve of the Fast of Holy Saint Jacob.\n16. Thursday. Tone [AZ]. [Feast of] Eustratius, Auxentius, etc. Canticle of the youths [Harts] [DK]: \"Who with wondrous...\"\n\nMay:\n13. Thursday. Tone [DK]. Ascension of Christ.\n23. Sunday. Tone [AK]. Coming of the Holy Spirit [Pentecost]. Eve of the Fast of Elijah.\n30. Sunday. Tone [AZ]. First. Beginning of the Sundays of the Resurrection. Canticle of the youths [Harts] [AZ]: \"Who came for our salvation.\"\n\nJuly:\n11. Sunday. Tone [BDZ]. Varstavar [Transfiguration]. The eating period [between fasts] is four weeks. Look in the First Volume up to Friday of the third week; and on Saturday come here and celebrate the feasts written below, which are after the Octave of the Theophany.\n31. Saturday. Tone [DCH]. [Feast of] Gregory the Theologian. Proper Hymn [ah.] [AK]: \"Who adorned...\" with its proper canons. Magnificat [Mkk] [B3]: \"Who with light.\"\n\nAugust:\n1. Sunday. Tone [DK]. Fourth. Canticle of the youths [Harts] [BK]: \"Who the heavenly hosts.\" Evening hymn [Hamb.] [DK]: \"When they came\" and \"The angel descended.\"\n2. Monday. Tone [AZ]. [Feast of] Vahan of Goghtn, Gordius, Polyeuctus, and Grigoris. Canticle of the youths [Harts] [DZ]: \"Holy art thou, Lord.\"\n3. Tuesday. Tone [AK]. [Feast of] Eugenia the Virgin, etc. Canticle of the youths [Harts] [DK]: \"To thee, O God.\"\n5. Thursday. Tone [BK]. [Feast of] Eugenius, Macarius, etc. Canticle of the youths [Harts] [DK]: \"Who with wondrous...\"\n7. Saturday. Tone [GK]. [Feast of] the Holy Ecumenical Council of Ephesus of the two hundred Patriarchs.\n8. Sunday. Tone [D-DZ]. Fifth. Canticle of the youths [Harts] [DZ]: \"We glorify thee.\" Evening hymn [Hamb.] [G3]: \"Preceding the women.\" Eve of the Fast of the Holy Mother of God.\n9. Monday. Tone [DK]. Fast of the Mother of God. Canticle of the youths [Harts] [B3]: \"Who didst save.\"\n15. Sunday. Tone [GK]. Assumption of the Holy Mother of God. The eating period [between fasts] is three weeks. Look in the First Volume, keeping the order of this place.\n\nSeptember:\n5. Sunday. Tone [BDZ]. Fourth. Canticle of the youths [Harts] [GK]: \"Ineffable.\" Evening hymn [Hamb.] [B3]: \"In the tomb...\"",
